# Read AGENTS.md and PROJECT_CONTEXT.md first

Before planning or implementing **any** task in this repository:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root in full: how to work (workflow, conventions).
2. Read `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` at the repository root in full: what exists (every
   endpoint, data model, business rule, configuration, test, and known gap).
3. Follow the mandatory workflow in `AGENTS.md` (explore, plan, implement, verify,
   update docs, report).
4. Apply its conventions for NestJS structure, ESM `.js` imports, DTO validation,
   Swagger docs, auth/security, config, error handling, and testing.

If a request conflicts with either file, ask the user before deviating. When you change
behaviour, update `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` (including its change history) in the same change;
when you introduce a new convention, update `AGENTS.md`.
